  "body": "Attempting to use the [create or modify user account](https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/latest/admin_api/user_admin_api.html#create-or-modify-account) admin api to add an external ID to a user that is already mapped to another user fails with a unique constraint db error. It should really return a HTTP 400 error instead.\r\n\r\nIn addition, any existing external IDs for the user that we were trying to modify will be erased (all entries for that user are removed from the `user_external_ids` table. This is due to the fact that the removal and addition of old and new IDs are separate actions:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/220f901229a506a82aedc51c5923768bf935ea4f/synapse/rest/admin/users.py#L285-L299\r\n\r\nThey should really be bundled into a single database transaction in a new storage function so that it's not possible for the user to be left without any mappings.",
